From 0f42b33b1227bf60abe6063b537f0eb2129e731e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:37:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Sample Thursday simulation and example season on Stats

- lib/league/simulate.ts: builds a throwaway league and runs made-up
  Thursdays through the REAL ledger (sign-up, Pick 7, seeded draw,
  scorecard save) so every point and chart is exactly what the live site
  would show. Deterministic per seed; never saved. Example Pick 7 players
  use made-up names. Showcase mode guarantees an own goal, a penalty, an
  assist, a floater, a fair-play loss and a missed rotation.
- /simulate?s=<seed>: "A sample Thursday" explainer in five steps: the
  draw, the scoresheet, what each rule did tonight, every player's
  itemised points, and the best and worst example Pick 7 teams with
  their breakdowns. "Simulate another Thursday" re-rolls.
- /stats?example=<seed>: the real Stats page rendered from an 8-week
  example season, under a clear "Example season" banner. The empty Stats
  page now offers it; Rules and the empty Table link to the simulation.

Tests: 96 (3 new in lib/league/simulate.test.ts).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PtuBR2yKPy8UddCaB5RWRB
